  "notes": "Saudi Cement Company (ticker 3030) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/425_0_2026-03-16...). Auditor: BDO Dr. Mohamed Al-Amri & Co. The consolidated financial statements were authorised to issue by the Board of Directors on 9 March 2026 (Note 36). Amounts are presented in thousands of Saudi Riyals (scale 1000). The five primary statements (printed FS pages 6-9) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.6x); the notes are digital text. Consolidated group; equity has no non-controlling interest (equity = share capital + retained earnings - the statutory reserve was transferred to retained earnings in FY2024 under the new Companies Law), and there are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies. investments_associates is 'Investment in an associate'; share_of_profit_associates is 'Share of profit of investment in an associate'. provisions is 'Provision for site restoration'. income_taxes_and_zakat is the single 'Zakat expense' line. other_current_liabilities combines 'Dividend payable' and 'Contract liabilities'; accrued_expenses is 'Accrued and other liabilities'; current_debt is 'Short term loans'; zakat_payable is 'Provision for Zakat'. depreciation_amortization sums 'Depreciation - property, plant and equipment', 'Depreciation - right of use assets' and 'Amortisation - intangible assets' from the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Additions to property, plant and equipment'; interest_paid is 'Finance cost paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'; dividends_paid is 'Dividend paid'. FY2025 was a softer year - cement demand and pricing eased so revenue was roughly flat at SAR 1.67bn while cost of revenue rose, taking gross margin from 39.8% to 36.1% and net income down 13.8% to SAR 363.7m. The cash-flow closing balance equals the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line exactly. Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: financial position 6, profit or loss and OCI 7, changes in equity 8, cash flows 9.",
